      {
        "id": 2598858148,
        "content": "I regularly create new repositories and try to price tasks, but we always need to first toggle some random label (the convention we follow is \"good first task\") and then the plug-in populates the rest. \nThe problem with this is that it's not intuitive. We should listen for when a new issue is filed and check if the labels are populated already. \nIf they aren't then we should populate. I think that this flow is more intuitive for new partners.  \nOr ideally, this plug-in should change the organization repository's default labels so that when a new repository created, they are already pre-populated but I'm not sure if this is straightforward or worth extending our permissions for if we don't already have them.",
